UART0 of RTL8197F (not-VG) does not follow the standard layout of 16550.

The receive/transmit register is located at offset +0x024 from the base UART0, and not +0x000,
and the word length field in LCR occupies the 0 bit rather than the [1:0] bits. Driver 8250 accesses
to registers using constants from this header, so without editing the console goes silent
exactly at the moment when early printk passes the output to the real driver.

Confirmations (not a hypothesis):
  * vendor bspchip.h from Realtek SDK v3.6.0: BSP_UART0_THR_8197F = BASE+0x024,
    BSP_CHAR_LEN_8 = 0x01 (not 0x03);
  * dump ROM-loader of the device itself: procedure for displaying a symbol at the address
    0x80000474 polls LSR and makes sb to 0xB8147024, and unconditionally -
    There is no chip variant check in the bootloader at all. The device console is working,
    This means our specimen is the 8197F variant (not VG), which has THR to +0x024.

Edit taken from 303-rtl8197f-uart.patch fork openwrt-AC10, shortened: hunk with
UART_IIR_ID is thrown away because for CONFIG_RTL_8197F=y it sets the same value
0x0e, which is already in the vanilla kernel.

The patch was generated from the Linux 4.14.275 reference tree rather than edited by
hand, so its context matches that source revision.

--- a/include/uapi/linux/serial_reg.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/serial_reg.h
@@ -18,8 +18,13 @@
 /*
  * DLAB=0
  */
+#ifdef CONFIG_RTL_8197F
+#define UART_RX		9	/* In:  Receive buffer */
+#define UART_TX		9	/* Out: Transmit buffer */
+#else
 #define UART_RX		0	/* In:  Receive buffer */
 #define UART_TX		0	/* Out: Transmit buffer */
+#endif
 
 #define UART_IER	1	/* Out: Interrupt Enable Register */
 #define UART_IER_MSI		0x08 /* Enable Modem status interrupt */
@@ -109,8 +114,13 @@
 #define UART_LCR_STOP		0x04 /* Stop bits: 0=1 bit, 1=2 bits */
 #define UART_LCR_WLEN5		0x00 /* Wordlength: 5 bits */
 #define UART_LCR_WLEN6		0x01 /* Wordlength: 6 bits */
+#ifdef CONFIG_RTL_8197F
+#define UART_LCR_WLEN7		0x00 /* Wordlength: 7 bits */
+#define UART_LCR_WLEN8		0x01 /* Wordlength: 8 bits */
+#else
 #define UART_LCR_WLEN7		0x02 /* Wordlength: 7 bits */
 #define UART_LCR_WLEN8		0x03 /* Wordlength: 8 bits */
+#endif
 
